{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/925861-pledge-crafting-help","id":925861,"title":"Pledge crafting help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-04T06:31:08-07:00","id":925861,"title":"Pledge crafting help","content":"Hi, just ported over from the White wolf boards, and wanted an opinion on a pledge concept. I've got a player that has a character that is currently mortal and is looking to possibly go into changeling. The group (all currently mortals) will be given the opportunity to go to a Goblin Market, and I'm trying to even out the pledge craft to be evened out. How would you all even out a long term change like that with obligations to the Hobgoblin (or possibly a Weakened True Fae). Also, what would the equivalent experience be for just the Changeling Template?<br /> <br /> Thanks,<br /> <br /> Vitkiraven","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12078-vitkiraven","name":"vitkiraven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T08:19:33-07:00","id":925904,"title":"","content":"Is this Changeling 1e or 2e, the pledge rules work very differently depending on edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T08:54:06-07:00","id":925924,"title":"","content":"I haven't made the jump yet to 2e, so 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12078-vitkiraven","name":"vitkiraven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T10:43:04-07:00","id":925973,"title":"","content":"Show me what you've got so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T14:49:18-07:00","id":926099,"title":"","content":"Alright, here's what I got:<br /> Tasks:<br /> Hob/Fae: Ensorcellment -2 <br /> Proto-Changeling: Medial Endeavor (Continual usage of the Mind Reading merits that the PC currently has to police thought for the Hob) -2<br /> Tied at -2 each<br /> Boons:<br /> Hob/Fae: Adroitness (help with Persuasion skills) +1, Favor, Lesser +1 (One time lesser favor later)<br /> Proto-Changeling: Ensorcellment +2 (so that he can know what he has to deal with)<br /> Tied at 0 currently<br /> Sanction:<br /> Hob/Fae: Poisoning of boon: Adroitness -1, Favor -1<br /> Proto-Changeling: Ensorcellment Poisoning -2<br /> Back to -2 each<br /> Duration:<br /> Month: Both +2<br /> Back to 0 each.<br /> I think I remember that it takes more than a week to have a changeling shift over.<br /> My main issue is that the Changeling template isn't included as a task, boon, or sanction so I can't really see a good price. This does go right along with a Faustian bargain concept but is it balanced enough with that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12078-vitkiraven","name":"vitkiraven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T06:28:25-07:00","id":926375,"title":"","content":"I'm assuming the mortal/PC is spending that week-or-so with the hob/fae in the Hedge/Arcadia, yeah? It's usually necessary to spend some time in Arcadia to become a 'ling (and usually with a Fae). But everything has the caveat of &quot;usually;&quot;, there aren't very hard-and-fast rules for becoming a Changeling.<br /> <br /> In terms of picking up the template, you could treat it as a Greater boon (+3), with some heavy sanctions or tasks on the human's side. It could also be something that the person just picks up; they don't notice their brain swelling and skin greying until they get back from their temporary job.<br /> <br /> Balance-wise, I'm not sure how to rank the cost of a template; are all the players getting templates? If so, no problem, pretend the templates are balanced; if not...well, Changelings get one free specialty (3xp), five free Contract dots (15-60xp, depending on what you buy), one dot of Wyrd (8xp), permanent enscorcelment (4xp, based on the Enchanted Mortal merit), one dot of Mantle (2xp), general access to the Hedge and Glamour (call it 6xp?), seeming and kith blessings (varies a lot, call it 10xp). That comes to a total of 48-93xp, call it 90xp to have a round number.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T06:56:34-07:00","id":926383,"title":"","content":"Thanks Ace,<br /> I was kind of thinking that the PC wouldn't straight up be removed from play, but be stuck in either the Hedge or Arcadia for the period of time, setting it up that the PC will get the deal with the Merchant, go into a back room, and a Fetch comes out for him to continue play. Also, thank you for the Experience Breakdown. I was having trouble coming up with a fair Experience value for Pledge-Crafting, Dream access and what not.<br /> Also, I couldn't find it anywhere, but is there anywhere that describes a transition from Morality (or Integrity) to Clarity for rankings? This character is currently sitting precariously at 4, so should it be a straight carryover?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12078-vitkiraven","name":"vitkiraven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T09:21:17-07:00","id":926455,"title":"","content":"There's also the option of &quot;time shenanigans;&quot; the character may feel like they're gone for a month, but from the other character's perspective, it's a day (assuming the player didn't want to mess with being a fetch, or whatever).<br /> <br /> As far as translating Morality, I personally would do it straight. 1e Clarity has a number of sins in common with Morality, and while they measure different things, it seems fairer to do it straight (particularly since both cost xp to raise, so giving a raise/hit when becoming a Changeling throws xp calcs out of wack, and may not feel fair).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T10:20:08-07:00","id":926486,"title":"","content":"Clarity is alien compared to mortality so I'd just start the Changeling at 7 clarity, easy that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T10:31:06-07:00","id":926495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/925861-pledge-crafting-help?p=926486#post926486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clarity is alien compared to mortality so I'd just start the Changeling at 7 clarity, easy that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. 1e Clarity is mostly morality with a few things tacked on: don't stop interacting with regular people, don't break your word, and don't get unpleasantly surprised. You still have your standard don't kill, don't steal, don't wave magic in front of people. And giving Clarity 7 (from Morality 4) is effectively gifting 54xp. (First edition: you can buy back your sense of right and wrong, but it'll cost ya!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T10:47:52-07:00","id":926510,"title":"","content":"Good point, I concede.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T11:17:31-07:00","id":926533,"title":"","content":"Good point on the time Shenanigans. I might make it that this Merchant is eternal, but that their personal time is sped up dramatically. <br /> Working the math out again:<br /> Alright, here's what I got:<br /> Tasks:<br /> Hob/Fae: Make the PC a Changeling (-3)<br /> Proto-Changeling: a Year of the PC's Life (-2) seems about right?<br /> Boons:<br /> Hob/Fae: Favors, Median +3 (requiring 3 of them should jump it up one position, rather than be counted 3 times, and requiring 3 favors sounds changeling like)<br /> Proto-Changeling: Becoming a Changeling +3 (I'd say without Contracts being truncated)<br /> Sanction:<br /> Hob/Fae: Curse: Adroitness (Social) -1<br /> Proto-Changeling: Poisoned Enspelling: -2 (certainly can't make him mortal again)<br /> Duration:<br /> A day: Both +1<br /> Back to 0 each.<br /> <br /> Seem legit?<br /> Thanks on the Clarity/Morality (since this PC likes to use Mind-Reading/Mind Breaker I don't know how long it will last at that level though).<br /> <br /> Also, I think I remember this somewhere, but can you mix Seemings and Kiths?<br /> I'd think that He'd gravitate towards a whisperwisp for kith but Fairest for seeming. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12078-vitkiraven","name":"vitkiraven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T12:00:07-07:00","id":926548,"title":"","content":"I forget if it says this specifically in RAW, but generally, benefits from a Pledge fade after the Pledge ends. True Fae are specifically called out to be able to break that rule, but hobs aren't. Personally, I would go with the first version you had, with the side effect being that the PC turns into a Changeling. <br /> <br /> As to the pledge itself: is the &quot;year of a PC's life&quot; a year of service, or a year's worth or lifeforce? I'd argue the former would require the duration be a year, even if ironside it only lasts for a day. Three Medial Favors is a +6 per RAW, all counted separately. Three Lesser Favors would be +3. What do you mean by &quot;without Contracts being truncated&quot;? And what does &quot;Poison Enspelling&quot; do, mechanically? Same as poisoned Enscorcelment?<br /> <br /> Also, if I were the ST, I would have the character lose the mind-reading merits once they were a Changeling, as stacking templates feels thematically and mechanically messy. I'd say replace them with a Kith/Contract that did something similar, but I can't think of any mind-reading ones in 1e (Fleeting Court Contracts kinda work...)<br /> <br /> Per the core, Kiths map directly to Seemings. The Spring splat book introduced an optional rule that decoupled them (meaning you can have whatever Kith with whatever Seeming). I personally like being able to mix and match, though with ST oversight to prevent gratuitous min-maxing or thematic collision (a lot of the Beast and Elemental Kiths don't play well with other Seemings without severe re-writes of flavor).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T16:48:54-07:00","id":926718,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I had meant Ensorcelment. As for the contracts, I was going to give the Changeling Template without the Contracts, and have the PC buy them later, probably with XP from the Merits. The Character is a Psychologist that is a bit on the evil side. He works in a Hospital usually on night shift so maybe the Dream Contracts for the Mind Reading and The Lunacy based ones for the Mind Breaker Merit.<br /> The year of the PC's life was a year taken away, whether it is at the end or the year he developed the merits I hadn't worked out yet, but it was a year taken, not served, which was why I had lowered the value.<br /> The Merchant could easily be a Fallen True Fae, I hadn't decided which would be best yet.<br /> I think if he has the Whisperwisp Kith, with the Fairest Seeming, with Dream and Lunacy Contracts it should simulate what he can do now with a bit more flexibility, so a net positive for him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12078-vitkiraven","name":"vitkiraven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T13:16:37-07:00","id":927754,"title":"","content":"Does a pledge's words have to all be in the same language? Would a True Fae use multiple languages to make a pledge sound like something completely different?<br /> My example: A heavily accented phrase sounding like &quot;You is a seeking&quot; Pronounced &quot;Yue is za asiq um&quot; - Using multiple languages could be Yue (Chinese for 1 month) is (Azerbaijani for work) za (Bosnian word for for) asiq (Kazakh for open) um (Bosnian for Mind), roughly One month of work for an open mind?<br /> Did that make sense at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12078-vitkiraven","name":"vitkiraven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T14:03:52-07:00","id":927775,"title":"","content":"There's nothing in RAW that says it has to be, but all the examples given are in English only, so...<br /> <br /> In my opinion, that kind of calculated word trap seems more human (or Demon) than fae, given that it relies on complicated linguistics and a knowledge of the technical working of language. Gentry have trouble with human minutae; they do stories well, and a bit of wordplay, but not at that level. I would err on the side of phrasing that is misleading, but less obtuse than that. Something like, &quot;I'll ask a task a day, in exchange for expanding your mind and horizons. You'll return before the moon fills again.&quot; Or, &quot;Hey, you've got a heck of a talent. You mind giving me a bit of your time? I promise, it's safe stuff, I'll owe you for it, and it won't take more than a month.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T16:40:02-07:00","id":927833,"title":"","content":"Good points. I was thinking along the lines of the Merchant being an Exiled Fae with their Personal time being much faster than normal, That would give them a lot of time to perfect this kind of thing, but it would also put them as more human. If the advanced time thing was in play, would the Merchant even bother with it, being that they would like to hide any downsides of a bargain (from what I read of Goblin Markets).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12078-vitkiraven","name":"vitkiraven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}